{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_bugfix_short_blind_call_target", "label": "Bugfix: Short-Stacked BB Call Target Set to Posted Amount Instead of Configured Blind", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/BUGFIX_short_blind_call_target.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-04-28", "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_bugfix_short_blind_call_target_tda_rule_41", "label": "TDA Rule 41 (short all-in BB: call target stays at configured blind)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/BUGFIX_short_blind_call_target.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Standard cardroom rule: an all-in-for-less BB does not discount the call; chip conservation is preserved by pot stratification (main pot capped at the all-in, side pots above it, single-contestant excess returned uncalled). The 0.0.48 change conflated 'BB can only win the all-in amount' with 'callers commit only the all-in amount'."}, {"id": "docs_bugfix_short_blind_call_target_pot_stratification", "label": "Pot stratification / uncalled-bet return invariant", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/BUGFIX_short_blind_call_target.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A winner's award from a pot layer is bounded by their commitment to that layer; folded contributions are awarded by layer but folders cannot win; a layer with a single contributor is uncalled and returned. Audit heuristic: never conflate what-actually-happened fields with rule-derived fields."}, {"id": "docs_bugfix_short_blind_call_target", "label": "Bugfix: Short Blind Call Target", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/BUGFIX_short_blind_call_target.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_bugfix_short_blind_call_target", "target": "docs_d